      "entryId": "1sa-2-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The adversaries of the LORD shall be broken to pieces; out of heaven shall he thunder upon them... and he shall give strength unto his king, and exalt the horn of his anointed. Hannah's song closes with the first occurrence of Mashiach in Scripture — centuries before a king exists in Israel. First principle: the anointed King is a promise before He is a person on a throne; broken adversaries and exalted strength converge on Christ.",
      "density": 3.2714,
      "words": 76,
      "sentences": 4,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
