    },
    {
      "entryId": "1sa-8-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The throne-rejection read as theocracy-rejection. First principle: asking for a king like the nations is a verdict on God's reign — and Hosea repeats the charge when Israel asks a king again.",
      "density": 2.3429,
      "words": 32,
